    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5125\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nauthorizing Congregation Talmud Torah D'Chasidei Bobov Monsey to file\nan application for a real property tax exemption\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo authorize Congrecation Talmund\nTorah D'Chasidei Bobov Monsey to file an application for a real\nproperty tax exemption.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 authorizes the town of\nRamapo, County of Rockland, to accept from Congregation Talmund Torah\nD'Chasidei Bobov Monsey an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nCongregation Talmund Torah D'Chasidei Bobov Monsey\nis a not-for-profit organization that would be entitled\nto such an exception if the organization filed an application\nfor the exemption by the appropriate taxable status date.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
